        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS take great pleasure in introducing to the market this substantial three-bedroom semi-detached family home, with the additional benefit of a converted attic and garage conversion, situated on Newlands Drive, Dublin 22.\nBoasting one of Clondalkin's most desirable addresses, this particular location is the cream of the crop. You are ideally positioned on the fringe of Clondalkin Village, with every conceivable amenity within walking distance, including convenience stores, bars and restaurants, and primary and secondary schools. You also benefit from immediate access to the N7 and M50 motorways, while the Red Cow Luas is found just a few minutes away by car.\nImmaculately presented, internal living accommodation of approximately 144 sq.m. can be found here and, in brief, consists of an entrance hall, living room, dining room, kitchen, second reception room/sunroom, and downstairs shower room on the ground floor.\nUpstairs, you will find three well-proportioned bedrooms, the family bathroom, and stair access to the converted attic, which also benefits from an ensuite bathroom.\nExternally, this property boasts a substantial EAST-facing rear garden with a patio area, large lawn, and timber shed, while the front offers a large block-paved driveway providing parking for a number of vehicles.\nNo. 7 comes to the market in fantastic condition from top to bottom and has been meticulously maintained, improved, and upgraded by its current owners.\nBased on its location, size, and condition, we know this one is going to be extremely popular with a variety of buyers. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers at your earliest convenience to avoid missing out on this fantastic opportunity to purchase a property in one of Clondalkin's finest addresses.\n\nFeatures\nPristine throughout\n144 Sq.m.\n3 bed, 3 bath\nConverted attic with ensuite\nConverted garage\nCondensing gas boiler\nSystemlink 3-zone heating system\nLuxury Jacuzzi jet bath\nOpen marble fireplace\nGas fire in dining room\nXL EAST-facing garden\nServices extended into rear garden\nPotential for future garden development\nFully insulated garden shed with electricity\nGarden shed approx. 4.3m × 2.3m\nLarge driveway to front\nSought-after location\nClose to amenities\nBER D\n\nTurn Key Family Home in Prime Clondalkin Location\nCall today to arrange a viewing!\n \n \n "
      },
